35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that offshore houses are about 5,400 yen per person, but food is extra! Also, all-in rates mean everyone pays the same regardless of how much they eat. That sounds a bit unfair, doesn't it?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your ""clear number"" just became complicated, didn't it? As for the travel, the ferry option is a disaster—it eats two whole days. I'm already leaning toward the city or the valley.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, it is not unfair; it is predictable. My research shows that separate room bookings last time caused a price gap of 8,000 yen. A single bill for a whole building is the only way to ensure absolute equality.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, I agree about the ferry, but the houses are worse. One bathroom for everyone and cold water? No way. I'm not dealing with that. We need a place with actual doors and flexible times.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, your concern about the layout is valid. My findings suggest that a shared house can feel suffocating because there is no escape for those needing a moment alone, whereas a town setting provides that natural breathing room.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, but if I eat less, I'm paying for someone else's huge dinner! That's not a clear number, that's just a mystery fee! Maybe the valley or city is better if we can just pay for what we use?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, you're contradicting yourself. Now you want to pay for what you use? Typical. Regardless, the city is the only rational choice for time. No planning, no waiting, and no wasted days. Why suffer through a schedule?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, paying for what you use sounds simple, but it creates a bookkeeping nightmare. Who tracks every single meal? A single, divided bill for a whole building eliminates the risk of someone quietly ending up out of pocket.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, you're right about the schedule. The inns have strict meal times and we'd all be crammed on futons in one room. That's a nightmare. A city room with a door is the only way to actually get some rest.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, @Takumi, it seems we are aligning on the city. Beyond the logistics, my research shows that last year's separate schedules left us disconnected. A city environment offers both group cohesion and the necessary space to avoid feeling crowded.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, bookkeeping is just a puzzle! I can help! But if the city has a clear total for the room and we just pay for our own snacks, that's the best of both worlds, right? No mystery fees!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, your ""puzzle"" is exactly why we should avoid complex bookkeeping. Let's be rational: the city minimizes transit time and eliminates the ferry's two-day waste. It's the only option that doesn't feel like a second job.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, your ""puzzle"" is exactly how people end up paying more than their share. If we choose the city, we must ensure the accommodation is a single flat or a fixed-rate block to avoid the price discrepancies I found.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, as long as we aren't all sleeping in one giant room on the floor, I don't care how you bill it. I just need a door and a schedule that isn't forced on me. The city is the only choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, a fixed-rate block in the city would satisfy your need for equality. It also solves the issue of feeling crowded; the urban environment allows us to be together while providing a natural exit for anyone needing a break.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, @Asuka, if we can find a city place with one fixed price for the room, I'm in! It sounds like the city is the winner for everyone. Let's do it!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Finally, some common sense. The city is the only option that doesn't treat our vacation like a logistics exercise. I'm satisfied as long as we aren't wasting our precious time waiting for ferries or buses.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Provided we secure a single booking with a fixed total to be divided equally, the city is the most logical choice. It satisfies the requirements for both efficiency and financial transparency.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm in. As long as we have separate rooms or at least a door and no strict meal times, the city is the only way to go. Let's just make sure we book it now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,It seems we have reached a consensus. The city provides the necessary balance: it prevents the isolation we felt last year while offering the personal space a shared house lacks. I vote for the city.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
